      en: "Fort Manda in Foulpointe (Mahavelona), located on the eastern coast north of Toamasina, is a massive circular coastal fortress built in the early 19th century. Constructed by the Merina King Radama I between 1822 and 1826 with the assistance of British military engineers, the fort was designed to defend the vital trading port against potential French naval attacks and to solidify Merina control over the eastern seaboard. Uniquely, the thick defensive walls, measuring up to 8 meters high, were constructed using a highly durable mortar made of coral powder, sand, and millions of egg whites. The fort is armed with original cast-iron cannons and stands as a formidable monument to the military modernization of the Merina Kingdom. Geschichte K8 — coastal defense and military engineering."
