      en: ["A massive circular coastal fortress located in Foulpointe (Mahavelona).", "Constructed by Merina King Radama I between 1822 and 1826.", "Built with the assistance of British military engineers to deter French attacks.", "The 8-meter-high walls were uniquely constructed using a mortar of egg whites.", "Designed to secure Merina control over the lucrative eastern seaboard trade.", "Features well-preserved original cast-iron cannons facing the ocean."]
