      en: ["Located on the small forested island of Nosy Mangabe in the Bay of Antongil.", "Served as a 16th and 17th-century safe anchorage for Dutch East India Company ships.", "Features rock carvings of sailor names, ship names, and dates of arrival.", "Acted as a physical 'post office' for fleets traveling to the East Indies.", "The rock inscriptions date back to the early 1600s.", "Represents some of the oldest European physical evidence on the eastern coast."]
